{#
  The modal that appears when the request has been refused.

  A single button, "ok", which goes to the showcase site's home page: the form is
  no longer in use, so there is nothing else to do from here. The PDF is a **link**
  inside the text, not an action to be put on a par with leaving.

  The text does not say **why** it was refused: that judgement is ours and the
  driver's. It says one thing, and it is one of three depending on the case
  (`rejection.case`, decided by `rejectionCase()` in src/server.js):

    out_of_scope     we are probably not the right tool. It holds for a request
                     that was understood and is too big for us.
    not_software     what was asked for is not software. Here we say what webtools
                     builds, and name a few examples of what it does not.
    not_recognised   the system did not recognise the request as a valid one. It
                     holds when there was nothing to judge: telling the user we are
                     not the right tool would make them believe their request had
                     been read and set aside.

  It opens by itself when the page loads (`rejection.js`), because it is the answer
  to the submission the user has just made: it is not a window appearing without
  their having asked for anything.
#}

{% macro render(rejection) %}
      <dialog class="card login-dialog" id="rejection-dialog" aria-labelledby="rejection-dialog-title"
              data-rejection-dialog data-home="{{ rejection.home_url }}">
        <div class="card-head login-dialog-head" id="rejection-dialog-title">{{ t("preanalyst.rejection." ~ rejection.case ~ ".title") }}</div>
        <div class="login-dialog-body">
          <p class="login-dialog-lead">{{ t("preanalyst.rejection." ~ rejection.case ~ ".lead") }}</p>
          <p class="login-dialog-hint">
            {{ t("preanalyst.rejection.pdf_hint") }}
            <a class="text-link" href="{{ rejection.pdf_url }}">{{ t("preanalyst.rejection.pdf_link") }}</a>
          </p>
          <form method="dialog" class="login-dialog-close">
            <button class="btn btn-primary" type="submit" value="ok">{{ t("preanalyst.rejection.ok") }}</button>
          </form>
        </div>
      </dialog>
{% endmacro %}
